  "worked_solution": "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required conditional probability is given by\n\n$$\nP(X=2\\,|\\,Y=2)=\\frac{P(X=2,Y=2)}{P(Y=2)}=\\frac{f(2,2)}{{f}_{Y}(2)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal distribution of $Y.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(2) & =f(1,2)+f(2,2) \\\\  & =0.25+0.1 \\\\  & =0.35.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(2,2)=0.1.$ \n\nFinally, substituting ${f}_{Y}(2)=0.35$ and $f(2,2)=0.1$ in our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=2\\,|\\,Y=2) & =\\frac{f(2,2)}{{f}_{Y}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.1}{0.35} \\\\  & \u22480.29.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
